  "year": "1981",
  "subtitle": "A drafting-pantograph drawing tablet: trace a picture under Mylar and twin potentiometers in the arm's pivots translate your stroke into coordinates the computer replots as vector art.",
  "why_scout_cares": "The embodied inverse of a plotter. The same two-link pantograph mechanics used in CAD digitizers was sold to home users as an art tool — you physically trace under a clear sheet and the machine rebuilds your gesture on screen. The interaction is the mechanism itself: a 6-inch pivoting arm whose twin rotary potentiometers turn arm angles into X/Y points. A 1993 Atari Classics retrospective literally asks 'Should VersaWriter be in a museum?'",
  "search_terms": ["VersaWriter", "Versa Writer", "Versa Computing", "pantograph drawing tablet", "digitizer drawing board", "Atari VersaWriter"],
